        "original_id": "91a53518-1965-54b1-a551-a70312ab2380",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dean Jones, Laurens van der Post\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, NBC\n- Works: The Million Dollar Duck, The $1,000,000 Duck, A Far Off Place, A Far-Off Place, A Story Like the Wind, The Love Bug, Beethoven, Ensign O'Toole\n- Topics: American comedy films, adventure drama films, television military comedy\n\nFacts:\n- Ensign O'Toole was a military comedy television series that aired on NBC from September 23, 1962, to May 5, 1963.\n- Dean Jones, age 31, played the title role in Ensign O'Toole as a nonchalant United States Navy ensign during the early 1960s.\n- Dean Jones played Jim Douglas in The Love Bug in 1968.\n- The Million Dollar Duck, also titled The $1,000,000 Duck, is a 1971 American comedy film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Million Dollar Duck is about a goose that lays golden eggs.\n- Dean Jones played Albert Dooley in The Million Dollar Duck in 1971 and received a Golden Globe nomination for that role.\n- Laurens van der Post wrote A Story Like the Wind in 1972 and A Far-Off Place in 1974.\n- A Far Off Place is a 1993 American adventure drama film based on Laurens van der Post's works A Far-Off Place and its prequel A Story Like the Wind.\n- Dean Jones played Dr. Herman Varnick in Beethoven in 1992.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
